      "a": "Mendel found out that following things in the pea plant:\nIt had some traits which come in pairs. Like the seed is either rough or smooth. It is either yellow or green, and the height of the plant is either tall or short.\nThe next generation (the children) of a plant will also be either rough or smooth. There is no seed which is mixed– a bit smooth and a bit rough.\nHe found the same with colour. Seeds which are either green or yellow give rise to new seeds which are either green or yellow.\nThe next generation does not have seeds with a mixed new colour made from both green and yellow.\nMendel showed that in the next generation of pea plants there will be more plants having yellow seeds. He also showed that the next generation will have more plants with smooth seeds."
